Placeholder so `wheelhouse/` exists in every checkout: the Dockerfile COPYs it unconditionally so a
disconnected site can stage wheels into it, and `COPY` of a missing directory fails the build.

Stage the wheels here with

    python scripts/check_offline_install.py --wheelhouse wheelhouse

then build with

    docker build --build-arg INSTALL_MODE=wheelhouse --tag mdqm:local .

The wheels themselves are deployment artefacts; `.gitignore` keeps them out of the repository.
